const decisions={
'flashcard:mfa':['Recognize that MFA combines different authentication-factor types.','Qualified bounded acronym/definition card. Its password-plus-authenticator example is a knowledge/possession example under the intended authenticator assumptions, not two knowledge secrets or a guarantee of phishing resistance. Both faces are mounted; flipping changes visual/aria-hidden state. Manual flip and a6.2-second timer reveal teaching; reduced motion disables auto-flip, and the timer is not conditioned on in-view state. No grading or recall mastery is demonstrated.'],
'lesson-prompt:dns-attacks':['Prompt the learner to distinguish poisoned resolution from traffic tunneling.','Qualified only as a comparison prompt, not a full lesson, detection rule or evidence of either attack. Forged/corrupted DNS answers and using DNS as a communications channel differ; observing a suspicious DNS record alone cannot establish either. No packet clues, controls or learner check are delivered here.'],
'lesson-prompt:phishing':['Direct attention to urgency, claimed identity and communications channel as phishing clues.','Qualified as a bounded attention prompt. A clue is not proof: legitimate messages can be urgent and phishing can appear calm or familiar. Independent verification is still needed. This preview provides no message analysis task, safe-link assessment, full phishing lesson or completed learner test.'],
'lesson-prompt:web-attacks':['Prompt tracing untrusted input to a possible execution context.','Qualified only as an injection-oriented analysis cue within a broad web-attacks topic. Not all web attacks execute injected code; CSRF, access-control failures and other mechanisms require different reasoning. No payload, application assessment, output-context remediation, full lesson or test is delivered.'],
'mcq:solution-explanation':['Explain the minimum-needed-access purpose of least privilege.','Qualified standalone solution teaching. It is visible immediately in a separate explanation showcase; focus clicks only emphasize it. Role here describes necessary access and does not approve a precise RBAC mapping. It does not make the leaking MCQ or complete three-choice feedback valid.'],
'mcq:distractor-explanation':['Contrast physical-entry tailgating with an authorization principle.','Qualified standalone explanation of the named physical-access distractor. It is always visible and emphasis is optional. It supplies neither a complete account of physical access nor rationale for the other MCQ distractor, and it is not conditionally attached to the learner-selected wrong answer.'],
'mcq:access-control':['Recognize least privilege among the three illustrated labels.','HOLD: no supported native guest identity/payload adapter. Answer-key CSS classes are always present and hover/active colors reveal correctness before an answer click; a separate explanation card also already states the concept. Clicks grade immediately and retries are unlimited. Recognition can be discussed, but this is assisted demonstration, not independent or trusted assessment.'],
'mcq:feedback':['Provide immediate verdict/retry status after a choice.','HOLD complete feedback: the two wrong choices receive the identical generic retry, with no selected-misconception rationale. The correct status is only a short minimum-access cue. The separate explanation showcase is not wired to answer state and covers only one distractor, so it cannot be silently merged into complete per-choice feedback.'],
'pbq:incident-response-ordering':['Illustrate a simplified containment/cleanup/recovery dependency.','HOLD: unsupported native guest namespace, no actual question-shaped payload contract, and no incident/plan premises justify a universal linear response sequence. A keyed next-step highlight aids completion before grading. The actual plain-text drop handler accepts unknown strings and marks all nonempty slots complete; full sequence correctness is coarse and supplies no separate skill or incident-response mastery.'],
'pbq:hint':['Expose the internal expected value for the next empty slot.','HOLD as qualified distinct teaching: this is an answer-bearing highlight, not a rationale or explicitly labeled guided-learning mode. It is present before response and depends on a fixed index key rather than validation of the whole prefix. After some wrong placements it can disappear. It cannot establish unassisted novelty, a correct response plan or separate teaching efficacy.'],
'pbq:feedback':['Display a coarse complete-sequence verdict and containment-first cue.','HOLD: all five wrong legal permutations get the same retry. One already starts with containment, so that retry misdiagnoses its actual recovery/cleanup ordering error. Neither every step nor why recovery/eradication belong in the particular sequence is explained. Successful placement and the secured wording do not prove containment or a real incident result.'],
'review-path:iam':['Show an illustrative identity/access topic path.','HOLD full displayed record: fixed percentage, recent-miss signal, priority and spacing labels are presented as detected accuracy and highest-impact adaptation without learner-history input or a visible synthetic-data label in the preview. Access minimization, federation and MFA are different topics, not measured weaknesses or proven prerequisites.'],
'review-path:logs':['Show an illustrative logging-to-response topic path.','HOLD full displayed record: the local dictionary drives every metric and step, while the interface claims detected accuracy and a rebuilt adaptive queue. No log evidence, learner miss history, impact ranking or real spaced schedule is used. Plausible topic order alone cannot validate those claims or a response finding.'],
'review-path:pki':['Show an illustrative certificate-trust topic path.','HOLD full displayed record: fabricated measurement provenance is unresolved. The fixed path can name roots, chains and validation, but it neither evaluates certificates nor measures a learner. No actual trust decision, diagnostic precision, calculated priority or spaced-retention result is approved.']};
